@startuml
left to right direction
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

actor Guest
actor Parent
actor Specialist
actor Admin

rectangle "SEN Support Platform" {
  usecase "SC-01\nRegister, sign in, and establish session" as SC01
  usecase "SC-02\nView or update linked child profile" as SC02
  usecase "SC-03\nPlan, view, update, or cancel support session" as SC03
  usecase "SC-04\nCreate and read diary entries" as SC04
  usecase "SC-05\nInspect permitted diary version history" as SC05
  usecase "SC-06\nView permitted audit events" as SC06
  usecase "SC-07\nManage accounts and specialist assignments" as SC07
  usecase "SC-08\nExport permitted child records" as SC08
}

Guest --> SC01
Parent --> SC01
Specialist --> SC01
Admin --> SC01

Parent --> SC02
Specialist --> SC02
Admin --> SC02

Parent --> SC03
Specialist --> SC03

Parent --> SC04
Specialist --> SC04

' SC-05 has no explicit permission row in the access matrix; no actor association is inferred.
Parent --> SC06
Admin --> SC06

Parent --> SC07
Admin --> SC07

Parent --> SC08

note bottom of SC01
Guest access is limited to registration, sign-in,
and public pages. Public pages are included in SC-01.
end note

note bottom of SC02
Admin can view child profile metadata only.
Parent and Specialist require a valid child relationship.
end note

note bottom of SC07
Parent association is limited to specialist assignments
as primary guardian; it does not include account management.
Pending confirmation.
end note

note bottom of SC08
Parent export requires a linked child and primary guardian rights;
only permitted records are exported.
end note
@enduml
